stories=[
 dict(slug='the-market-before-noon',number='01',title='The Market Before Noon',deck='A few good things, chosen slowly.',eyebrow='The Market',image='/assets/images/31-market-produce-crates.webp',inline='/assets/images/32-selecting-produce.webp',intro='The first ingredient is attention. Before the pan warms, before a knife touches the board, there is the small ritual of choosing what to bring home.',sections=[('Look closer','A market has its own way of telling time. Crates are stacked, leaves curl at their edges, and someone knows exactly which tomato has reached its moment. The strongest colour is not always the best clue: texture, weight and a gentle fragrance can say more.','For this imagined story, the market is an editorial setting rather than a documented place. The point is the pleasure of paying attention to the everyday.'),('Leave room for surprise','A shopping list is useful, but it does not have to close the door on curiosity. One bunch of herbs can change a plan. A handful of ripe tomatoes can make dinner feel entirely different.','A good meal often starts with a simple question: what looks good today?'),('Bring it to the table','Back at home, wash what needs washing, store delicate leaves with care and let the best ingredients do most of the work. That is the spirit of this first volume: less spectacle, more flavour.')]),
 dict(slug='an-ode-to-the-lemon',number='02',title='An Ode to the Lemon',deck='The smallest way to change everything.',eyebrow='Ingredient Notes',image='/assets/images/33-lemon-branch-still-life.webp',inline='/assets/images/34-zest-lemon.webp',intro='Sometimes a dish does not need another hour. It needs a few drops of brightness.',sections=[('Two kinds of brightness','A lemon brings both juice and zest. The juice tastes sharp and immediate; its peel carries fragrant oils that can make a dish feel vividly alive. They do different jobs, and knowing when to use each changes the result.','Zest first, before cutting the fruit, and keep the bitter white pith out of your finely grated peel.'),('A small finishing gesture','Try a squeeze of lemon at the very end of a bean dish, after tasting the salt. Add fine zest to cake batter, or let a few drops sharpen a dressing that tastes flat.','The goal is balance, not making everything taste of lemon.'),('Keep it simple','There is a particular pleasure in working with an ingredient that is so familiar. It takes very little to notice it again.')]),
 dict(slug='the-good-pantry',number='03',title='The Good Pantry',deck='A little less, a little better.',eyebrow='The Everyday Shelf',image='/assets/images/35-everyday-pantry.webp',inline='/assets/images/04-bread-and-crumb.webp',intro='A useful pantry is not a museum of perfectly matching jars. It is a quiet collection of things that make an ordinary dinner possible.',sections=[('Start with what you use','Dry pasta, rice, beans, chickpeas, good olive oil and a few seasonings can open more doors than an overflowing cupboard of forgotten ingredients. Choose what you genuinely cook, then replenish it as you go.','Decanting into clean jars can make quantities easy to see, but keeping the original packaging information nearby helps with dates, ingredients and allergens.'),('Everyday combinations','Beans become a lemony lunch. Rice welcomes a handful of herbs. Pasta can carry last night’s roasted peppers. A modest shelf is enough to support a lot of different meals.'),('Order without performance','Keep dry ingredients cool and dry, check dates and follow package storage instructions. The useful pantry is the one you can cook from, not the one that photographs best.')]),
 dict(slug='the-table-after',number='04',title='The Table After',deck='What remains when the meal is over.',eyebrow='Around the Table',image='/assets/images/36-clearing-the-table.webp',inline='/assets/images/06-after-lunch-table.webp',intro='The nicest part of a meal is not always the first bite. Sometimes it is the minute afterward, when nobody quite wants to leave.',sections=[('A small gathering','A table can hold a lot without being crowded. A plate passed along, a little bread torn rather than sliced, a conversation that changes direction. Nothing here needs to be perfect.','The traces left behind say something that a pristine place setting never can: someone was here, and they stayed a while.'),('Ordinary rituals','Clearing the plates is part of the rhythm. We stack bowls, gather glasses and notice what has disappeared. It is an ending, but a gentle one.'),('Make room','Cooking can be about the food, of course. It can also be a way of making space for people to feel at home. That is the kind of everyday table MESA wants to celebrate.')])
]
(ROOT/'content/recipes.json').write_text(json.dumps(recipes,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
(ROOT/'content/stories.json').write_text(json.dumps(stories,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Created',len(recipes),'recipes &',len(stories),'stories')
